# M3.5.1 Control CI diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-27
Run: `33089488278`
Status: resolved in feature branch; exact-head rerun required

## Failure

The first Control workflow run failed only in its final static cron check. The
check scanned every historical file below `scripts/` and therefore found
`scripts/tu1nz_m1_infra_gate.sh`, which contains the previously documented
legacy Cron-to-systemd migration command. All restore verifier tests, Python
compile, shell syntax and manifest JSON validation had already passed.

## Cause

The new check was broader than the M3.5.1 change and incorrectly treated a
pre-existing migration artifact as a new restore implementation defect.

## Correction and rollback

The workflow now scans only the three new restore runtime artifacts for cron
behavior. It does not modify or excuse the historical migration file. Rollback
is revert of the exact workflow correction commit; no server or runtime state
was changed.
